<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb refined lead output falls 1.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb refined lead output falls 1.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese refined lead output in February fell a seasonally adjusted 1.5 percent from the prior month, according to Ministry of International Trade and Industry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, output was up 2.2 percent year-on-year at 18,644 tonnes.</p>
<p>The February data was as follows (in tonnes, percent):</p>
<p>		 Feb 97     Jan 97   y/y change  s/a change*</p>
<p> Output	18,644     19,674     + 2.2	 - 1.5</p>
<p> Shipments   19,189     18,618     +13.1	 + 5.5</p>
<p> Stocks	13,708     14,809     -18.1	 -10.3</p>
<p>(*Seasonally adjusted change, month-on-month)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
